      "message": "fix(2d): contour arc fit passes each vertex on the wall's air side\n\nA coarse contour fit (tolerance 0.1) let a vertex stand 0.05 mm off its\ncircle toward the part. The verifier forgives 0.01 mm, so a tessellated\nround wall walked clockwise posted arcs that verify held as gouges.\nWalls that know their part side (closed rings, open chains, the lead\nreseat) now fit one-sided: the circle keeps the run's end vertices and\nits centre slides along their bisector until no vertex is on the part\nside.\n\nFixes #1579\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
