      "message": "fix(2d): sided arc fit keeps true circles and refuses split pieces off the circle\n\nThe held one-sided fit counted any vertex 1e-9 mm on the part side, so\nexact holes, bores and the M8 boss lost their closed-ring arcs and seven\ngolden tests failed. A vertex within ARC_SIDE_SLACK (1e-3 mm, ten times\nunder the verifier's GOUGE_TOL) now keeps the two-sided circle; only a\nvertex past it moves the centre or refuses the arc. Every golden test\npasses unchanged.\n\nA sweep over half a turn posts as pieces that end on interior vertices.\nA sided fit now takes only split vertices on the circle: the\nconventional walk of the Ø30 fixture posted a piece that ended 0.05 mm\noff its circle and verify held it as a gouge. A sided fit also looks\npast up to 4 refused run ends, so a faceted wall fits 3 arcs a level,\nnot 22-32. The compensation part contour fits sided too.\n\nFixes #1579\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
